counterfactuals.output:
1. A flexible pipe connector (200) for connecting a pressurized mains pipe to a service pipe, the flexible pipe connector (200) comprising:
* an elongate corrugated body extending along a longitudinal axis, the corrugated body comprising a plurality of alternating peaks and troughs;
* a first spigot socket disposed at a first longitudinal end of the corrugated body and configured to couple to the pressurized mains pipe; and
* a second spigot socket disposed at an opposing second longitudinal end of the corrugated body and configured to couple to the service pipe;
* wherein an internal diameter defined by the inner surfaces of the troughs of the corrugated body is substantially equal to an internal diameter of the first spigot socket and an internal diameter of the second spigot socket; and
* wherein the geometry of the peaks and troughs and the internal diameter of the corrugated body are configured such that a fluid head loss across the flexible pipe connector (200) during pressurized fluid flow therethrough is substantially equivalent to a fluid head loss of a rigid, smooth-bore pipe having an equivalent length and internal diameter.
